<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cătellus</span></b> , i,
		m., and far more freq. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cătella</span></b>  (once not contr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cătēnŭla</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. 26, 462</span></i>),
		ae, f.
		dim.
		catena; cf. <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 556</span></i> P.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a small chain.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>Masc.</i>, in a play on the meaning of 1. catellus,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 5, 3,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>Fem.</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 135,
			1</span></i>; Caecil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 199, 10</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 17, 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				31, 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vaginae catellis crepitant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 12, 54, § 152</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 19, 31, 15</span></i>,
			and <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 273, 12</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
